  "c5_structural_blocker": "C5 (GEO-GOLDEN-LO vs GEO-GOLDEN-HI) is NOT RUN, and the reason is structural rather than budgetary. The golden index floor requires N >= F(17)^2 = 2,550,409 lattice points before the emergent parastichy stride behaves like phi at all. A 16-degree box at 0.25 degree resolution contains 65 x 65 = 4,225 cells -- three orders of magnitude below the floor. GEO-GOLDEN-HI therefore CANNOT be constructed at box scale on this grid, so the comparison the bar asks for has no admissible high arm. Reported rather than faked with an interpolated sub-grid lattice, which would sample the interpolator and not the field."
